  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nI need to identify the lede in the semantic content of an HTML document.\n\nImagine a page generated by Apache httpd's mod_autoindex, containing a list of HTML documents. Each document in the list should have a title (html/head/title) and a lede (html/???/????) that appears in the resulting index.\n\nHow would an Apache filter identify the lede in a correctly formatted html document?\n\nNote that for this purpose there is no need to support any wild west HTML, if you want mod_autoindex to show the lede to you, format your HTML correctly, if you have wild west HTML there is no lede and that is fine. The question here is, what is \"correctly\"?\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\nNone that I can find.\n\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\nDecide on the what defines the lede: html/????/????\n\nWhat are the values of ????\n\n### Anything else?\n\nI plan on extending mod_autoindex or something like it, and in the process this will create a de-facto standard. I don't want to create standards, I want to follow them.\n",
